":"GB","home":false,"pf":31.0,"pa":0.0,"off_snaps":70,"epa_per_play":0.2993,"pass_rate":0.4857,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5484,"def_epa_per_play":-0.3633}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2021,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.5626,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Mike LaFleur"},{"season":2023,"team":"BUF","distance":0.5834,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"BUF","distance":0.6051,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Joe Brady"},{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":0.6386,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.6442,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Brian Daboll"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LA","distance":0.9637,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Raheem Morris"},{"season":2018,"team":"GB","distance":0.984,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"PHI","distance":0.9899,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2019,"team":"MIA","distance":0.9914,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Patrick Graham"},{"season":2020,"team":"TEN","distance":0.9921,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Lions went 6-10 in 2018 and were outscored 360 to 324. The offense ranked 23rd in EPA per play and the defense 21st in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. What set them apart was the 2nd highest 10 personnel usage and the highest Cover 1 rate in the league.","offense":"The Lions offense was well below average by EPA per play. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Schematically, they stood out for the 2nd highest 10 personnel usage and the 3rd fewest tight ends on the field in the league. Matthew Stafford ran the passing game, with Kenny Golladay leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Lions defense was a little below average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 13th and 23rd. Romeo Okwara led the team with 7.5 sacks, and Eli Harold added 4 despite playing only 26% of the snaps. Schematically, they had the highest Cover 1 rate in the league.","special":"The Lions were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 88% of field goals, which was a little above average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Matthew Stafford played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 3,777 yards. Targets were spread around, with Kenny Golladay and Theo Riddick leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield was a committee led by LeGarrette Blount and Kerryon Johnson. On defense, Romeo Okwara led the team with 7.5 sacks and Quandre Diggs picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2021 Jets under Mike LaFleur and the 2023 Bills. Their defense looked most like the 2023 Rams under Raheem Morris and the 2018 Packers.","trends":"2018 is the first season covered here, so there is no earlier year to compare it with. The charts below show how the Lions changed over the seasons that followed.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2018. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}